{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018fPcyEyzzdsrnjNBvxsVuj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"id\": \"QuantAgent-375\",\n3\t  \"title\": \"Scope replay signal lookup to selected source run\",\n4\t  \"description\": \"Integration review of QuantAgent-3o8 found that `Backtest.run_replay()` loads signals only by symbol/timeframe/date/environment and does not reliably scope them to the selected source BacktestRun.\\n\\nEvidence:\\n- Feature branch: `feature/QuantAgent-3o8-implement-replay-execution-mode-reuse-an`\\n- Replay proof run on 2026-05-10 showed source run 1 consuming signal ID 2 from a different overlapping run because `signal_map[(symbol, generated_at)]` was overwritten.\\n- Acceptance criteria TC5/TC11 require the replay to use the same source-run signals and keep the provenance chain traceable.\\n\\nRequired change:\\n1. Add or derive a robust signal-to-source-run linkage (explicit `backtest_run_id` on `Signal` or another deterministic provenance key already persisted).\\n2. Update replay signal loading to query only the selected source run.\\n3. Add tests covering overlapping runs with identical symbol/timeframe/timestamp to prevent cross-run signal contamination.\\n4. Revalidate replay provenance and no-LLM behavior before re-routing integration.\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- New replay UI features\\n- Parallel replay execution\\n- Broader backtest refactors\",\n5\t  \"status\": \"open\",\n6\t  \"priority\": 1,\n7\t  \"issue_type\": \"bug\",\n8\t  \"owner\": \"fscheu@gmail.com\",\n9\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-05-10T21:43:21.793527211Z\",\n10\t  \"created_by\": \"Federico Scheu\",\n11\t  \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-10T21:43:21.793527211Z\",\n12\t  \"dependencies\": [\n13\t    {\n14\t      \"id\": \"QuantAgent-3o8\",\n15\t      \"title\": \"Implement Replay execution mode (reuse analyses without LLM calls)\",\n16\t      \"description\": \"## Context\\nRequirement D in trading_system_requirements.md specifies that backtests should support 'replay execution' - reusing stored analyses with different Portfolio/Risk profiles without re-calling LLMs.\\n\\n## Current State\\n- BacktestRun stores config_snapshot and analyses with checkpoints\\n- Signal model has thread_id, checkpoint_id, state_snapshot fields\\n- No replay execution mode implemented\\n- UI Replay tab exists but execution is not functional\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- Can select a completed backtest_run with stored analyses\\n- Can select one or multiple different portfolio/risk profiles\\n- Replay executes using stored analyses (no new LLM calls)\\n- Two executions over same analysis set but different profiles yield distinct P&L/metrics\\n- Comparison view shows side-by-side metrics and equity curves\\n\\n## Technical Notes\\n- Implement in Backtest class or separate ReplayExecutor\\n- Sequential execution for multiple profiles (MVP decision)\\n- Reference: docs/03_design/strategy_assembler_architecture.md\",\n17\t      \"status\": \"blocked\",\n18\t      \"priority\": 2,\n19\t      \"issue_type\": \"feature\",\n20\t      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T19:24:13.22456169Z\",\n21\t      \"created_by\": \"baiscf\",\n22\t      \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-10T21:43:41.550890492Z\",\n23\t      \"labels\": [\n24\t        \"backtesting\",\n25\t        \"mvp\",\n26\t        \"openclaw:design_approved\",\n27\t        \"replay\"\n28\t      ],\n29\t      \"dependency_type\": \"discovered-from\"\n30\t    }\n31\t  ]\n32\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f08f8d0e-dfe1-47d6-abdf-e601734c006c","uuid":"8904f81b-f3b4-4e7e-bd2d-c1036fd2674a","timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:39:01.992Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-375/20260511T073839Z-QuantAgent-375-planner/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"QuantAgent-375\",\n  \"title\": \"Scope replay signal lookup to selected source run\",\n  \"description\": \"Integration review of QuantAgent-3o8 found that `Backtest.run_replay()` loads signals only by symbol/timeframe/date/environment and does not reliably scope them to the selected source BacktestRun.\\n\\nEvidence:\\n- Feature branch: `feature/QuantAgent-3o8-implement-replay-execution-mode-reuse-an`\\n- Replay proof run on 2026-05-10 showed source run 1 consuming signal ID 2 from a different overlapping run because `signal_map[(symbol, generated_at)]` was overwritten.\\n- Acceptance criteria TC5/TC11 require the replay to use the same source-run signals and keep the provenance chain traceable.\\n\\nRequired change:\\n1. Add or derive a robust signal-to-source-run linkage (explicit `backtest_run_id` on `Signal` or another deterministic provenance key already persisted).\\n2. Update replay signal loading to query only the selected source run.\\n3. Add tests covering overlapping runs with identical symbol/timeframe/timestamp to prevent cross-run signal contamination.\\n4. Revalidate replay provenance and no-LLM behavior before re-routing integration.\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- New replay UI features\\n- Parallel replay execution\\n- Broader backtest refactors\",\n  \"status\": \"open\",\n  \"priority\": 1,\n  \"issue_type\": \"bug\",\n  \"owner\": \"fscheu@gmail.com\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-05-10T21:43:21.793527211Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"Federico Scheu\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-10T21:43:21.793527211Z\",\n  \"dependencies\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"QuantAgent-3o8\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Replay execution mode (reuse analyses without LLM calls)\",\n      \"description\": \"## Context\\nRequirement D in trading_system_requirements.md specifies that backtests should support 'replay execution' - reusing stored analyses with different Portfolio/Risk profiles without re-calling LLMs.\\n\\n## Current State\\n- BacktestRun stores config_snapshot and analyses with checkpoints\\n- Signal model has thread_id, checkpoint_id, state_snapshot fields\\n- No replay execution mode implemented\\n- UI Replay tab exists but execution is not functional\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- Can select a completed backtest_run with stored analyses\\n- Can select one or multiple different portfolio/risk profiles\\n- Replay executes using stored analyses (no new LLM calls)\\n- Two executions over same analysis set but different profiles yield distinct P&L/metrics\\n- Comparison view shows side-by-side metrics and equity curves\\n\\n## Technical Notes\\n- Implement in Backtest class or separate ReplayExecutor\\n- Sequential execution for multiple profiles (MVP decision)\\n- Reference: docs/03_design/strategy_assembler_architecture.md\",\n      \"status\": \"blocked\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"feature\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-19T19:24:13.22456169Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"baiscf\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-05-10T21:43:41.550890492Z\",\n      \"labels\": [\n        \"backtesting\",\n        \"mvp\",\n        \"openclaw:design_approved\",\n        \"replay\"\n      ],\n      \"dependency_type\": \"discovered-from\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JkLn36wNb3j6q43RqkTjY4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md\n2\t\n3\tThis file provides guidance to coding agents when working in this repository.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## Project Overview\n8\t\n9\t**QuantAgent** is a multi-agent trading analysis system that uses vision-capable LLMs (Claude, GPT-4, Qwen) to analyze financial markets in high-frequency trading (HFT) contexts. It combines technical indicators, candlestick pattern recognition, and trend analysis through a LangGraph-orchestrated agent pipeline.\n10\t\n11\t**Reference Paper:** arXiv:2509.09995 - \"Price-Driven Multi-Agent LLMs for High-Frequency Trading\"\n12\t\n13\t---\n14\t\n15\t## Repository Structure\n16\t\n17\tThis repository is organized around three main axes:\n18\t1. Core trading / backtesting engine (`quantagent/`)\n19\t2. Applications and interfaces (`apps/`)\n20\t3. Documentation, planning, and operational context (`docs/`, `.beads/`)\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t### quantagent/ — Core Engine & Domain Logic\n25\t\n26\tMain Python package containing all trading, backtesting, and agent logic.\n27\t\n28\t#### Agent & Graph Core\n29\t- `agent_state.py` — LangGraph shared state schema\n30\t- `agent_models.py` — Agent-related domain models\n31\t- `agent_utils.py` — Shared utilities for agents\n32\t- `graph_setup.py` — LangGraph StateGraph definition\n33\t- `trading_graph.py` — Main orchestrator (LLM providers, graph execution)\n34\t- `default_config.py` / `settings.py` — Configuration defaults\n35\t\n36\t#### Market Analysis Agents\n37\t- `indicator_agent.py` — Technical indicators (RSI, MACD, etc.)\n38\t- `pattern_agent.py` — Candlestick pattern detection (vision LLM)\n39\t- `trend_agent.py` — Trend & support/resistance analysis\n40\t- `decision_agent.py` — Final LONG / SHORT / HOLD decision\n41\t\n42\t#### Backtesting\n43\t- `backtesting/`\n44\t  - `backtest.py` — Backtest execution engine\n45\t\n46\t#### Strategy & 