{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_013ekqZ7CktaqqXAcso9Ws3d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of the current state. The `Signal` model on `main` does NOT have a `backtest_run_id` column - that was presumably added on the feature branch `feature/QuantAgent-3o8-implement-replay-execution-mode-reuse-an`. Let me check the feature branch to see what was added there.\n\nActually, the issue is that the tech-lead rejected the 3o8 implementation because of signal contamination. The implementer report said they added `replay_source_run_id` FK on `BacktestRun`, but the `Signal` model still doesn't have a `backtest_run_id` to link signals to their source run.\n\n\nThe core problem is in `run_replay()` - it loads signals by `(symbol, generated_at)` key, which causes collisions when multiple runs have overlapping signals, overwriting the map. I need to add `backtest_run_id` to the `Signal` model so signals are properly linked to their source run, which will fix the contamination issue.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the implementation plan: I'll need to add the column to the model, create a migration, update the signal creation methods to set the backtest run ID, modify the replay query to filter by source run, and add tests for the cross-run contamination scenario. Since this is the planning phase, I should focus on documenting the approach rather than writing code. Let me check what existing design and acceptance test docs are already in place to avoid duplicating work. I need to check the existing design docs that reference replay and backtest functionality to understand how the current architecture handles these patterns before I start writing the new documentation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5449,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13039,"cache_read_input_tokens":36610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input