{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EzUyMv8ARNjeaRVHdi1FN5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Backtesting Engine - Technical Documentation\n2\t\n3\t## Overview\n4\t\n5\tThe QuantAgent backtesting engine validates trading strategies by simulating execution on historical data. It combines data caching, analysis execution, trade simulation, and performance metrics calculation.\n6\t\n7\t**Location**: `quantagent/backtesting/` and `quantagent/data/`\n8\t\n9\t**Key Components**:\n10\t- `Backtest` - Main backtesting orchestrator\n11\t- `DataProvider` - Data caching layer (10x faster backtesting)\n12\t- `BacktestMetrics` - Performance metrics dataclass\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## Architecture\n17\t\n18\t```\n19\t┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n20\t│                     Backtest Engine                         │\n21\t└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n22\t                              │\n23\t        ┌─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐\n24\t        │                     │                     │\n25\t        ▼                     ▼                     ▼\n26\t┌───────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐\n27\t│ DataProvider  │     │ TradingGraph  │     │ OrderManager │\n28\t│ (Caching)     │     │ (Analysis)    │     │ (Execution)  │\n29\t└───────────────┘     └───────────────┘     └──────────────┘\n30\t        │                     │                     │\n31\t        │                     │                     │\n32\t        ▼                     ▼                     ▼\n33\t┌───────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐\n34\t│   MarketData  │     │    Signals    │     │    Trades    │\n35\t│   (Cache DB)  │     │   (Analysis)  │     │    (P&L)     │\n36\t└───────────────┘     └───────────────┘     └──────────────┘\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\t### Workflow\n40\t\n41\t1. **Date Range Iteration** - Loop through historical dates at specified timeframe\n42\t2. **Data Fetching** - DataProvider fetches OHLC data (from cache or API)\n43\t3. **Analysis Execution** - TradingGraph executes multi-agent analysis\n44\t4. **Trade Simulation** - OrderManager simulates order execution with slippage\n45\t5. **Portfolio Tracking** - PortfolioManager updates positions and P&L\n46\t6. **Metrics Calculation** - Calculate win rate, Sharpe, drawdown, etc.\n47\t7. **Result Persistence** - Store BacktestRun, Signals, Trades in database\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## Components\n52\t\n53\t### 1. Backtest Class\n54\t\n55\t**File**: `quantagent/backtesting/backtest.py`\n56\t\n57\tMain orchestrator for backtesting flow.\n58\t\n59\t#### Initialization\n60\t\n61\t```python\n62\tfrom quantagent.backtesting.backtest import Backtest\n63\t\n64\tbacktest = Backtest(\n65\t    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n66\t    end_date=datetime(2024, 3, 31),\n67\t    assets=['BTC', 'SPX'],\n68\t    timeframe='4h',\n69\t    initial_capital=100000.0,\n70\t    config={\n71\t        'base_position_pct': 0.05,\n72\t        'max_daily_loss_pct': 0.05,\n73\t        'max_position_pct': 0.10,\n74\t        'slippage_pct': 0.01\n75\t    },\n76\t    use_checkpointing=True\n77\t)\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t#### Parameters\n81\t\n82\t| Parameter | Type | Description | Default |\n83\t|-----------|------|-------------|---------|\n84\t| `start_date` | datetime | Backtest start date | Required |\n85\t| `end_date` | datetime | Backtest end date | Required |\n86\t| `assets` | List[str] | Asset symbols to backtest | Required |\n87\t| `timeframe` | str | Analysis timeframe (1h, 4h, 1d, etc.) | Required |\n88\t| `initial_capital` | float | Starting portfolio value | Required |\n89\t| `config` | Dict | Portfolio/risk/model configuration | `{}` |\n90\t| `db_session` | Session | Database session (creates if None) | `None` |\n91\t| `use_checkpointing` | bool | Enable LangGraph checkpointing | `False` |\n92\t\n93\t#### Methods\n94\t\n95\t**`run(name: Optional[str] = None) -> BacktestMetrics`**\n96\t\n97\tExecute backtest and return metrics.\n98\t\n99\t```python\n100\tmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"Q1 2024 Backtest\")\n101\t\n102\tprint(f\"Win Rate: {metrics.win_rate:.2%}\")\n103\tprint(f\"Total P&L: ${metrics.total_pnl:,.2f}\")\n104\t```\n105\t\n106\t**`get_equity_curve() -> pd.DataFrame`**\n107\t\n108\tGet equity curve as DataFrame.\n109\t\n110\t```python\n111\tequity_df = backtest.get_equity_curve()\n112\tequity_df.to_csv('equity_curve.csv')\n113\t```\n114\t\n115\t---\n116\t\n117\t### 2. DataProvider Class\n118\t\n119\t**File**: `quantagent/data/provider.py`\n120\t\n121\tCache-aside pattern for market data. Checks database first, fetches from yfinance API if missing, stores fetched data.\n122\t\n123\t#### Pattern\n124\t\n125\t```\n126\tRequest → Check DB → Found? → Return\n127\t                  ↓ Not Found\n128\t              Fetch API → Store DB → Return\n129\t```\n130\t\n131\t#### Usage\n132\t\n133\t```python\n134\tfrom quantagent.data.provider import DataProvider\n135\tfrom quantagent.database import SessionLocal\n136\t\n137\tprovider = DataProvider(SessionLocal())\n138\t\n139\tdf = provider.get_ohlc(\n140\t    symbol='BTC',\n141\t    timeframe='1h',\n142\t    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n143\t    end_date=datetime(2024, 1, 31)\n144\t)\n145\t```\n146\t\n147\t#### Key Features\n148\t\n149\t- **Gap Detection** - Identifies missing date ranges in cached data\n150\t- **Deduplication** - Avoids storing duplicate records\n151\t- **Symbol Mapping** - Maps custom symbols to yfinance format (BTC → BTC-USD)\n152\t- **Timeframe Conversion** - Converts timeframes to yfinance intervals\n153\t\n154\t#### Performance\n155\t\n156\t| Scenario | Time | Description |\n157\t|----------|------|-------------|\n158\t| **Cold Cache** | ~3 min | First run, fetches from API |\n159\t| **Warm Cache** | ~10 sec | Second run, reads from DB |\n160\t| **Speedup** | **18x** | Cache vs API |\n161\t\n162\t#### Cache Management\n163\t\n164\t```python\n165\t# Get cache statistics\n166\tstats = provider.get_cache_stats(symbol='BTC')\n167\tprint(f\"Total records: {stats['total_records']}\")\n168\t\n169\t# Clear cache\n170\tprovider.clear_cache(symbol='BTC')\n171\t```\n172\t\n173\t---\n174\t\n175\t### 3. BacktestMetrics Dataclass\n176\t\n177\t**File**: `quantagent/backtesting/backtest.py`\n178\t\n179\tPerformance metrics container.\n180\t\n181\t#### Fields\n182\t\n183\t| Field | Type | Description | Formula |\n184\t|-------|------|-------------|---------|\n185\t| `total_trades` | int | Total trades executed | Count |\n186\t| `winning_trades` | int | Trades with P&L > 0 | Count |\n187\t| `losing_trades` | int | Trades with P&L < 0 | Count |\n188\t| `win_rate` | float | Percentage of winning trades | winning_trades / total_trades |\n189\t| `profit_factor` | float | Ratio of wins to losses | sum(wins) / abs(sum(losses)) |\n190\t| `sharpe_ratio` | float | Risk-adjusted return | (return - rf) / volatility * sqrt(periods) |\n191\t| `max_drawdown` | float | Worst peak-to-trough decline | max((peak - trough) / peak) |\n192\t| `total_pnl` | float | Total profit/loss | sum(all trade P&L) |\n193\t| `avg_win` | float | Average winning trade | sum(wins) / winning_trades |\n194\t| `avg_loss` | float | Average losing trade | sum(losses) / losing_trades |\n195\t| `largest_win` | float | Largest single win | max(wins) |\n196\t| `largest_loss` | float | Largest single loss | min(losses) |\n197\t| `total_return_pct` | float | Total return percentage | (total_pnl / initial_capital) * 100 |\n198\t\n199\t---\n200\t\n201\t## Database Schema\n202\t\n203\t### BacktestRun\n204\t\n205\tStores backtest configuration and results.\n206\t\n207\t```python\n208\tclass BacktestRun(Base):\n209\t    __tablename__ = \"backtest_runs\"\n210\t\n211\t    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n212\t    name = Column(String(200))\n213\t    timeframe = Column(String(10), nullable=False)\n214\t    assets = Column(JSON, nullable=False)  # [\"BTC\", \"SPX\", ...]\n215\t    start_date = Column(DateTime, nullable=False)\n216\t    end_date = Column(DateTime, nullable=False)\n217\t\n218\t    # Configuration snapshot (immutable)\n219\t    config_snapshot = Column(JSON, nullable=False)\n220\t\n221\t    # Results (populated after run)\n222\t    total_trades = Column(Integer)\n223\t    win_rate = Column(Float)\n224\t    profit_factor = Column(Float)\n225\t    sharpe_ratio = Column(Float)\n226\t    max_drawdown = Column(Float)\n227\t    total_pnl = Column(Numeric(18, 8))\n228\t\n229\t    created_at = Column(DateTime, default=datetime.utcnow)\n230\t```\n231\t\n232\t**Config Snapshot Structure**:\n233\t\n234\t```json\n235\t{\n236\t  \"initial_capital\": 100000.0,\n237\t  \"base_position_pct\": 0.05,\n238\t  \"max_daily_loss_pct\": 0.05,\n239\t  \"max_position_pct\": 0.10,\n240\t  \"slippage_pct\": 0.01,\n241\t  \"model_provider\": \"openai\",\n242\t  \"model_name\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n243\t  \"temperature\": 0.1,\n244\t  \"use_checkpointing\": true\n245\t}\n246\t```\n247\t\n248\t### Signal (Modified for Backtesting)\n249\t\n250\tSignals generated during backtest have `environment = 'backtest'`.\n251\t\n252\t```python\n253\tclass Signal(Base):\n254\t    # ... existing fields ...\n255\t\n256\t    # Environment tag\n257\t    environment = Column(Enum(Environment), nullable=False, default=Environment.BACKTEST)\n258\t\n259\t    # Provenance - link to order created from this signal\n260\t    order_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"orders.id\"), nullable=True)\n261\t\n262\t    # Model metadata\n263\t    model_provider = Column(String(50))\n264\t    model_name = Column(String(100))\n265\t    temperature = Column(Float)\n266\t\n267\t    # Checkpoint integration\n268\t    thread_id = Column(String(100))\n269\t    checkpoint_id = Column(String(100))\n270\t```\n271\t\n272\t### Order (Modified for Backtesting)\n273\t\n274\tOrders created during backtest have `environment = 'backtest'` and link to triggering signal.\n275\t\n276\t```python\n277\tclass Order(Base):\n278\t    # ... existing fields ...\n279\t\n280\t    # Environment tag\n281\t    environment = Column(Enum(Environment), nullable=False, default=Environment.BACKTEST)\n282\t\n283\t    # Provenance - link to signal that triggered this order\n284\t    trigger_signal_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"signals.id\"), nullable=True)\n285\t\n286\t    # Relationships\n287\t    trigger_signal = relationship(\"Signal\", foreign_keys=[trigger_signal_id])\n288\t```\n289\t\n290\t**Provenance Flow**:\n291\t```\n292\tAnalysis → Signal (id=123, environment=backtest)\n293\t             ↓\n294\t         Order (id=456, trigger_signal_id=123, environment=backtest)\n295\t             ↓\n296\t         Trade (id=789, order_id=456, environment=backtest)\n297\t```\n298\t\n299\t### Trade (Modified for Backtesting)\n300\t\n301\tTrades executed during backtest have `environment = 'backtest'` and link to order.\n302\t\n303\t```python\n304\tclass Trade(Base):\n305\t    # ... existing fields ...\n306\t\n307\t    # Environment tag\n308\t    environment = Column(Enum(Environment), nullable=False, default=Environment.BACKTEST)\n309\t\n310\t    # Link to order\n311\t    order_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"orders.id\"))\n312\t```\n313\t\n314\t---\n315\t\n316\t## Configuration\n317\t\n318\t### Portfolio & Risk Config\n319\t\n320\t```python\n321\tconfig = {\n322\t    # Position Sizing\n323\t    'base_position_pct': 0.05,  # 5% of portfolio per trade\n324\t\n325\t    # Risk Management\n326\t    'max_daily_loss_pct': 0.05,  # 5% max daily loss (circuit breaker)\n327\t    'max_position_pct': 0.10,  # 10% max position size\n328\t\n329\t    # Execution\n330\t    'slippage_pct': 0.01,  # 1% slippage simulation (±2% total)\n331\t\n332\t    # Model\n333\t    'agent_llm_provider': 'openai',\n334\t    'agent_llm_model': 'gpt-4o-mini',\n335\t    'agent_llm_temperature': 0.1\n336\t}\n337\t```\n338\t\n339\t### Timeframes\n340\t\n341\tSupported timeframes:\n342\t- `1m`, `5m`, `15m`, `30m` - Intraday (high frequency)\n343\t- `1h`, `4h` - Medium frequency (recommended for MVP)\n344\t- `1d` - Daily\n345\t- `1w`, `1mo` - Long-term\n346\t\n347\t---\n348\t\n349\t## Usage Examples\n350\t\n351\t### Basic Backtest\n352\t\n353\t```python\n354\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n355\tfrom quantagent.backtesting.backtest import Backtest\n356\t\n357\t# 90-day backtest\n358\tend_date = datetime.now()\n359\tstart_date = end_date - timedelta(days=90)\n360\t\n361\tbacktest = Backtest(\n362\t    start_date=start_date,\n363\t    end_date=end_date,\n364\t    assets=['BTC'],\n365\t    timeframe='4h',\n366\t    initial_capital=100000.0\n367\t)\n368\t\n369\tmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"BTC 90-Day Test\")\n370\t\n371\tprint(f\"Win Rate: {metrics.win_rate:.2%}\")\n372\tprint(f\"Sharpe Ratio: {metrics.sharpe_ratio:.2f}\")\n373\tprint(f\"Total Return: {metrics.total_return_pct:.2f}%\")\n374\t```\n375\t\n376\t### Multi-Asset Backtest\n377\t\n378\t```python\n379\tbacktest = Backtest(\n380\t    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n381\t    end_date=datetime(2024, 3, 31),\n382\t    assets=['BTC', 'SPX', 'CL'],  # Multiple assets\n383\t    timeframe='1h',\n384\t    initial_capital=100000.0\n385\t)\n386\t\n387\tmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"Q1 Multi-Asset\")\n388\t```\n389\t\n390\t### With Custom Config\n391\t\n392\t```python\n393\tcustom_config = {\n394\t    'base_position_pct': 0.02,  # Conservative 2% sizing\n395\t    'max_daily_loss_pct': 0.03,  # Strict 3% daily loss limit\n396\t    'max_position_pct': 0.05,  # Max 5% per position\n397\t    'slippage_pct': 0.015,  # 1.5% slippage\n398\t    'agent_llm_provider': 'anthropic',\n399\t    'agent_llm_model': 'claude-3-haiku',\n400\t    'agent_llm_temperature': 0.05\n401\t}\n402\t\n403\tbacktest = Backtest(\n404\t    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n405\t    end_date=datetime(2024, 3, 31),\n406\t    assets=['BTC'],\n407\t    timeframe='4h',\n408\t    initial_capital=100000.0,\n409\t    config=custom_config\n410\t)\n411\t\n412\tmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"Conservative BTC Strategy\")\n413\t```\n414\t\n415\t### With Checkpointing\n416\t\n417\t```python\n418\t# Enable state persistence for long backtests\n419\tbacktest = Backtest(\n420\t    start_date=datetime(2023, 1, 1),\n421\t    end_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),  # 1 year\n422\t    assets=['BTC'],\n423\t    timeframe='1h',\n424\t    initial_capital=100000.0,\n425\t    use_checkpointing=True  # Resume if interrupted\n426\t)\n427\t\n428\tmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"1-Year BTC Backtest\")\n429\t```\n430\t\n431\t### Querying Provenance\n432\t\n433\t```python\n434\tfrom quantagent.models import Signal, Order, Trade, Environment\n435\t\n436\t# Get all backtest orders with their triggering signals\n437\torders = db.query(Order).filter(\n438\t    Order.environment == Environment.BACKTEST\n439\t).all()\n440\t\n441\tfor order in orders:\n442\t    signal = order.trigger_signal\n443\t    print(f\"Order {order.id} triggered by Signal {signal.id}\")\n444\t    print(f\"  Model: {signal.model_provider}/{signal.model_name}\")\n445\t    print(f\"  Confidence: {signal.confidence}\")\n446\t\n447\t# Get all signals and their resulting orders\n448\tsignals = db.query(Signal).filter(\n449\t    Signal.environment == Environment.BACKTEST\n450\t).all()\n451\t\n452\tfor signal in signals:\n453\t    if signal.order_id:\n454\t        print(f\"Signal {signal.id} → Order {signal.order_id}\")\n455\t```\n456\t\n457\t---\n458\t\n459\t## Performance Metrics\n460\t\n461\t### Viability Criteria (MVP)\n462\t\n463\tStrategy is considered viable if:\n464\t- **Win Rate** ≥ 40%\n465\t- **Sharpe Ratio** ≥ 1.0\n466\t- **Max Drawdown** ≤ 15%\n467\t\n468\t### Interpretation\n469\t\n470\t| Metric | Good | Acceptable | Poor |\n471\t|--------|------|-----------|------|\n472\t| Win Rate | ≥ 50% | 40-50% | < 40% |\n473\t| Profit Factor | ≥ 2.0 | 1.5-2.0 | < 1.5 |\n474\t| Sharpe Ratio | ≥ 1.5 | 1.0-1.5 | < 1.0 |\n475\t| Max Drawdown | ≤ 10% | 10-15% | > 15% |\n476\t\n477\t---\n478\t\n479\t## Metrics Calculation Details\n480\t\n481\t### Sharpe Ratio\n482\t\n483\t```python\n484\t# Annualized Sharpe Ratio\n485\treturns = equity_curve.pct_change()\n486\texcess_return = returns.mean() - (risk_free_rate / periods_per_year)\n487\tsharpe = (excess_return / returns.std()) * sqrt(periods_per_year)\n488\t```\n489\t\n490\t**Periods per year**:\n491\t- 1h: 252 × 6.5 = 1,638 (trading days × hours per day)\n492\t- 4h: 252 × 1.625 = 410\n493\t- 1d: 252\n494\t- 1w: 52\n495\t\n496\t### Max Drawdown\n497\t\n498\t```python\n499\t# Percentage-based drawdown\n500\trunning_max = equity_curve.expanding().max()\n501\tdrawdown = (equity_curve - running_max) / running_max\n502\tmax_drawdown = abs(drawdown.min())\n503\t```\n504\t\n505\t### Profit Factor\n506\t\n507\t```python\n508\t# Ratio of gross profit to gross loss\n509\ttotal_wins = sum(pnl for pnl in trades if pnl > 0)\n510\ttotal_losses = abs(sum(pnl for pnl in trades if pnl < 0))\n511\tprofit_factor = total_wins / total_losses\n512\t```\n513\t\n514\t---\n515\t\n516\t## Testing\n517\t\n518\t### Unit Tests\n519\t\n520\t**DataProvider**: `tests/test_data_provider.py` (20 tests)\n521\t- Structure validation\n522\t- Cache-aside pattern\n523\t- Gap detection\n524\t- Symbol/timeframe mapping\n525\t- Edge cases\n526\t\n527\t**Backtest**: `tests/test_backtest.py` (30+ tests)\n528\t- Initialization\n529\t- Date range generation\n530\t- Metrics calculation (all formulas)\n531\t- Decision parsing\n532\t- Configuration snapshot\n533\t\n534\t### Integration Tests\n535\t\n536\t**Full Flow**: `tests/test_backtest_integration.py` (8 tests)\n537\t- End-to-end backtest execution\n538\t- Data fetching → Analysis → Execution → Metrics\n539\t- Risk manager integration\n540\t- Config snapshot reproducibility\n541\t- Equity curve tracking\n542\t\n543\t### Running Tests\n544\t\n545\t```bash\n546\t# All backtesting tests\n547\tpytest tests/test_data_provider.py tests/test_backtest.py -v\n548\t\n549\t# Integration tests\n550\tpytest tests/test_backtest_integration.py -v\n551\t```\n552\t\n553\t---\n554\t\n555\t## Best Practices\n556\t\n557\t### 1. Data Caching\n558\t\n559\tAlways use DataProvider for historical data:\n560\t- First run: ~3 minutes (fetches from API)\n561\t- Subsequent runs: ~10 seconds (reads from cache)\n562\t\n563\t### 2. Timeframe Selection\n564\t\n565\tRecommended timeframes by asset type:\n566\t- **Crypto** (BTC): 1h or 4h\n567\t- **Stocks** (SPX): 4h or 1d\n568\t- **Commodities** (CL): 4h\n569\t\n570\t### 3. Date Ranges\n571\t\n572\tMinimum backtest periods:\n573\t- **Development**: 1 month (quick validation)\n574\t- **Testing**: 3 months (strategy validation)\n575\t- **Production**: 1 year (robustness check)\n576\t\n577\t### 4. Configuration Management\n578\t\n579\tUse StrategyConfig model to persist profiles:\n580\t\n581\t```python\n582\tfrom quantagent.models import StrategyConfig\n583\t\n584\t# Create profile\n585\tconfig = StrategyConfig(\n586\t    name=\"conservative_crypto\",\n587\t    kind=\"combined\",\n588\t    json_config={\n589\t        'base_position_pct': 0.03,\n590\t        'max_daily_loss_pct': 0.02,\n591\t        # ...\n592\t    }\n593\t)\n594\tdb.add(config)\n595\tdb.commit()\n596\t\n597\t# Load profile\n598\tconfig = db.query(StrategyConfig).filter_by(name=\"conservative_crypto\").first()\n599\tbacktest = Backtest(config=config.json_config, ...)\n600\t```\n601\t\n602\t### 5. Checkpointing\n603\t\n604\tEnable for long backtests:\n605\t- Survives crashes\n606\t- Resume from last checkpoint\n607\t- Full execution history\n608\t\n609\t---\n610\t\n611\t## Troubleshooting\n612\t\n613\t### Issue: \"No data available\"\n614\t\n615\t**Cause**: Symbol not in cache, API fetch failed\n616\t\n617\t**Solution**:\n618\t```python\n619\t# Check cache status\n620\tstats = provider.get_cache_stats(symbol='BTC')\n621\tprint(stats)\n622\t\n623\t# Clear and re-fetch\n624\tprovider.clear_cache(symbol='BTC')\n625\tbacktest.run()\n626\t```\n627\t\n628\t### Issue: \"Backtest too slow\"\n629\t\n630\t**Cause**: Cold cache, many API calls\n631\t\n632\t**Solution**:\n633\t```python\n634\t# Pre-populate cache\n635\tfrom quantagent.data.provider import DataProvider\n636\tprovider = DataProvider(db)\n637\t\n638\tfor symbol in ['BTC', 'SPX', 'CL']:\n639\t    provider.get_ohlc(symbol, '1h', start, end)\n640\t\n641\t# Run backtest (now fast)\n642\tbacktest.run()\n643\t```\n644\t\n645\t### Issue: \"Zero trades executed\"\n646\t\n647\t**Cause**: Risk manager rejecting all trades\n648\t\n649\t**Solution**:\n650\t```python\n651\t# Check config\n652\tprint(backtest.config)\n653\t\n654\t# Relax limits temporarily for testing\n655\tconfig['max_position_pct'] = 0.50  # 50%\n656\tconfig['max_daily_loss_pct'] = 0.20  # 20%\n657\t```\n658\t\n659\t---\n660\t\n661\t## References\n662\t\n663\t- **Code**: `quantagent/backtesting/backtest.py`\n664\t- **Tests**: `tests/test_backtest.py`, `tests/test_backtest_integration.py`\n665\t- **Example**: `examples/run_backtest.py`\n666\t- **Requirements**: `docs/01_requirements/trading_system_requirements.md`\n667\t- **Data Caching**: `docs/03_technical/data_caching_architecture.md`\n668\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f08f8d0e-dfe1-47d6-abdf-e601734c006c","uuid":"7bd25797-f686-43f9-a92a-56fa7a78ff3e","timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:39:35.804Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/03_design/backtesting_engine.md","content":"# Backtesting Engine - Technical Documentation\n\n## Overview\n\nThe QuantAgent backtesting engine validates trading strategies by simulating execution on historical data. It combines data caching, analysis execution, trade simulation, and performance metrics calculation.\n\n**Location**: `quantagent/backtesting/` and `quantagent/data/`\n\n**Key Components**:\n- `Backtest` - Main backtesting orchestrator\n- `DataProvider` - Data caching layer (10x faster backtesting)\n- `BacktestMetrics` - Performance metrics dataclass\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     Backtest Engine                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                              │\n        ┌─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐\n        │                     │                     │\n        ▼                     ▼                     ▼\n┌───────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐\n│ DataProvider  │     │ TradingGraph  │     │ OrderManager │\n│ (Caching)     │     │ (Analysis)    │     │ (Execution)  │\n└───────────────┘     └───────────────┘     └──────────────┘\n        │                     │                     │\n        │                     │                     │\n        ▼                     ▼                     ▼\n┌───────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐\n│   MarketData  │     │    Signals    │     │    Trades    │\n│   (Cache DB)  │     │   (Analysis)  │     │    (P&L)     │\n└───────────────┘     └───────────────┘     └──────────────┘\n```\n\n### Workflow\n\n1. **Date Range Iteration** - Loop through historical dates at specified timeframe\n2. **Data Fetching** - DataProvider fetches OHLC data (from cache or API)\n3. **Analysis Execution** - TradingGraph executes multi-agent analysis\n4. **Trade Simulation** - OrderManager simulates order execution with slippage\n5. **Portfolio Tracking** - PortfolioManager updates positions and P&L\n6. **Metrics Calculation** - Calculate win rate, Sharpe, drawdown, etc.\n7. **Result Persistence** - Store BacktestRun, Signals, Trades in database\n\n---\n\n## Components\n\n### 1. Backtest Class\n\n**File**: `quantagent/backtesting/backtest.py`\n\nMain orchestrator for backtesting flow.\n\n#### Initialization\n\n```python\nfrom quantagent.backtesting.backtest import Backtest\n\nbacktest = Backtest(\n    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n    end_date=datetime(2024, 3, 31),\n    assets=['BTC', 'SPX'],\n    timeframe='4h',\n    initial_capital=100000.0,\n    config={\n        'base_position_pct': 0.05,\n        'max_daily_loss_pct': 0.05,\n        'max_position_pct': 0.10,\n        'slippage_pct': 0.01\n    },\n    use_checkpointing=True\n)\n```\n\n#### Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description | Default |\n|-----------|------|-------------|---------|\n| `start_date` | datetime | Backtest start date | Required |\n| `end_date` | datetime | Backtest end date | Required |\n| `assets` | List[str] | Asset symbols to backtest | Required |\n| `timeframe` | str | Analysis timeframe (1h, 4h, 1d, etc.) | Required |\n| `initial_capital` | float | Starting portfolio value | Required |\n| `config` | Dict | Portfolio/risk/model configuration | `{}` |\n| `db_session` | Session | Database session (creates if None) | `None` |\n| `use_checkpointing` | bool | Enable LangGraph checkpointing | `False` |\n\n#### Methods\n\n**`run(name: Optional[str] = None) -> BacktestMetrics`**\n\nExecute backtest and return metrics.\n\n```python\nmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"Q1 2024 Backtest\")\n\nprint(f\"Win Rate: {metrics.win_rate:.2%}\")\nprint(f\"Total P&L: ${metrics.total_pnl:,.2f}\")\n```\n\n**`get_equity_curve() -> pd.DataFrame`**\n\nGet equity curve as DataFrame.\n\n```python\nequity_df = backtest.get_equity_curve()\nequity_df.to_csv('equity_curve.csv')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. DataProvider Class\n\n**File**: `quantagent/data/provider.py`\n\nCache-aside pattern for market data. Checks database first, fetches from yfinance API if missing, stores fetched data.\n\n#### Pattern\n\n```\nRequest → Check DB → Found? → Return\n                  ↓ Not Found\n              Fetch API → Store DB → Return\n```\n\n#### Usage\n\n```python\nfrom quantagent.data.provider import DataProvider\nfrom quantagent.database import SessionLocal\n\nprovider = DataProvider(SessionLocal())\n\ndf = provider.get_ohlc(\n    symbol='BTC',\n    timeframe='1h',\n    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n    end_date=datetime(2024, 1, 31)\n)\n```\n\n#### Key Features\n\n- **Gap Detection** - Identifies missing date ranges in cached data\n- **Deduplication** - Avoids storing duplicate records\n- **Symbol Mapping** - Maps custom symbols to yfinance format (BTC → BTC-USD)\n- **Timeframe Conversion** - Converts timeframes to yfinance intervals\n\n#### Performance\n\n| Scenario | Time | Description |\n|----------|------|-------------|\n| **Cold Cache** | ~3 min | First run, fetches from API |\n| **Warm Cache** | ~10 sec | Second run, reads from DB |\n| **Speedup** | **18x** | Cache vs API |\n\n#### Cache Management\n\n```python\n# Get cache statistics\nstats = provider.get_cache_stats(symbol='BTC')\nprint(f\"Total records: {stats['total_records']}\")\n\n# Clear cache\nprovider.clear_cache(symbol='BTC')\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. BacktestMetrics Dataclass\n\n**File**: `quantagent/backtesting/backtest.py`\n\nPerformance metrics container.\n\n#### Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Description | Formula |\n|-------|------|-------------|---------|\n| `total_trades` | int | Total trades executed | Count |\n| `winning_trades` | int | Trades with P&L > 0 | Count |\n| `losing_trades` | int | Trades with P&L < 0 | Count |\n| `win_rate` | float | Percentage of winning trades | winning_trades / total_trades |\n| `profit_factor` | float | Ratio of wins to losses | sum(wins) / abs(sum(losses)) |\n| `sharpe_ratio` | float | Risk-adjusted return | (return - rf) / volatility * sqrt(periods) |\n| `max_drawdown` | float | Worst peak-to-trough decline | max((peak - trough) / peak) |\n| `total_pnl` | float | Total profit/loss | sum(all trade P&L) |\n| `avg_win` | float | Average winning trade | sum(wins) / winning_trades |\n| `avg_loss` | float | Average losing trade | sum(losses) / losing_trades |\n| `largest_win` | float | Largest single win | max(wins) |\n| `largest_loss` | float | Largest single loss | min(losses) |\n| `total_return_pct` | float | Total return percentage | (total_pnl / initial_capital) * 100 |\n\n---\n\n## Database Schema\n\n### BacktestRun\n\nStores backtest configuration and results.\n\n```python\nclass BacktestRun(Base):\n    __tablename__ = \"backtest_runs\"\n\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n    name = Column(String(200))\n    timeframe = Column(String(10), nullable=False)\n    assets = Column(JSON, nullable=False)  # [\"BTC\", \"SPX\", ...]\n    start_date = Column(DateTime, nullable=False)\n    end_date = Column(DateTime, nullable=False)\n\n    # Configuration snapshot (immutable)\n    config_snapshot = Column(JSON, nullable=False)\n\n    # Results (populated after run)\n    total_trades = Column(Integer)\n    win_rate = Column(Float)\n    profit_factor = Column(Float)\n    sharpe_ratio = Column(Float)\n    max_drawdown = Column(Float)\n    total_pnl = Column(Numeric(18, 8))\n\n    created_at = Column(DateTime, default=datetime.utcnow)\n```\n\n**Config Snapshot Structure**:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"initial_capital\": 100000.0,\n  \"base_position_pct\": 0.05,\n  \"max_daily_loss_pct\": 0.05,\n  \"max_position_pct\": 0.10,\n  \"slippage_pct\": 0.01,\n  \"model_provider\": \"openai\",\n  \"model_name\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n  \"temperature\": 0.1,\n  \"use_checkpointing\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Signal (Modified for Backtesting)\n\nSignals generated during backtest have `environment = 'backtest'`.\n\n```python\nclass Signal(Base):\n    # ... existing fields ...\n\n    # Environment tag\n    environment = Column(Enum(Environment), nullable=False, default=Environment.BACKTEST)\n\n    # Provenance - link to order created from this signal\n    order_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"orders.id\"), nullable=True)\n\n    # Model metadata\n    model_provider = Column(String(50))\n    model_name = Column(String(100))\n    temperature = Column(Float)\n\n    # Checkpoint integration\n    thread_id = Column(String(100))\n    checkpoint_id = Column(String(100))\n```\n\n### Order (Modified for Backtesting)\n\nOrders created during backtest have `environment = 'backtest'` and link to triggering signal.\n\n```python\nclass Order(Base):\n    # ... existing fields ...\n\n    # Environment tag\n    environment = Column(Enum(Environment), nullable=False, default=Environment.BACKTEST)\n\n    # Provenance - link to signal that triggered this order\n    trigger_signal_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"signals.id\"), nullable=True)\n\n    # Relationships\n    trigger_signal = relationship(\"Signal\", foreign_keys=[trigger_signal_id])\n```\n\n**Provenance Flow**:\n```\nAnalysis → Signal (id=123, environment=backtest)\n             ↓\n         Order (id=456, trigger_signal_id=123, environment=backtest)\n             ↓\n         Trade (id=789, order_id=456, environment=backtest)\n```\n\n### Trade (Modified for Backtesting)\n\nTrades executed during backtest have `environment = 'backtest'` and link to order.\n\n```python\nclass Trade(Base):\n    # ... existing fields ...\n\n    # Environment tag\n    environment = Column(Enum(Environment), nullable=False, default=Environment.BACKTEST)\n\n    # Link to order\n    order_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"orders.id\"))\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration\n\n### Portfolio & Risk Config\n\n```python\nconfig = {\n    # Position Sizing\n    'base_position_pct': 0.05,  # 5% of portfolio per trade\n\n    # Risk Management\n    'max_daily_loss_pct': 0.05,  # 5% max daily loss (circuit breaker)\n    'max_position_pct': 0.10,  # 10% max position size\n\n    # Execution\n    'slippage_pct': 0.01,  # 1% slippage simulation (±2% total)\n\n    # Model\n    'agent_llm_provider': 'openai',\n    'agent_llm_model': 'gpt-4o-mini',\n    'agent_llm_temperature': 0.1\n}\n```\n\n### Timeframes\n\nSupported timeframes:\n- `1m`, `5m`, `15m`, `30m` - Intraday (high frequency)\n- `1h`, `4h` - Medium frequency (recommended for MVP)\n- `1d` - Daily\n- `1w`, `1mo` - Long-term\n\n---\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n### Basic Backtest\n\n```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom quantagent.backtesting.backtest import Backtest\n\n# 90-day backtest\nend_date = datetime.now()\nstart_date = end_date - timedelta(days=90)\n\nbacktest = Backtest(\n    start_date=start_date,\n    end_date=end_date,\n    assets=['BTC'],\n    timeframe='4h',\n    initial_capital=100000.0\n)\n\nmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"BTC 90-Day Test\")\n\nprint(f\"Win Rate: {metrics.win_rate:.2%}\")\nprint(f\"Sharpe Ratio: {metrics.sharpe_ratio:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Total Return: {metrics.total_return_pct:.2f}%\")\n```\n\n### Multi-Asset Backtest\n\n```python\nbacktest = Backtest(\n    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n    end_date=datetime(2024, 3, 31),\n    assets=['BTC', 'SPX', 'CL'],  # Multiple assets\n    timeframe='1h',\n    initial_capital=100000.0\n)\n\nmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"Q1 Multi-Asset\")\n```\n\n### With Custom Config\n\n```python\ncustom_config = {\n    'base_position_pct': 0.02,  # Conservative 2% sizing\n    'max_daily_loss_pct': 0.03,  # Strict 3% daily loss limit\n    'max_position_pct': 0.05,  # Max 5% per position\n    'slippage_pct': 0.015,  # 1.5% slippage\n    'agent_llm_provider': 'anthropic',\n    'agent_llm_model': 'claude-3-haiku',\n    'agent_llm_temperature': 0.05\n}\n\nbacktest = Backtest(\n    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n    end_date=datetime(2024, 3, 31),\n    assets=['BTC'],\n    timeframe='4h',\n    initial_capital=100000.0,\n    config=custom_config\n)\n\nmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"Conservative BTC Strategy\")\n```\n\n### With Checkpointing\n\n```python\n# Enable state persistence for long backtests\nbacktest = Backtest(\n    start_date=datetime(2023, 1, 1),\n    end_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),  # 1 year\n    assets=['BTC'],\n    timeframe='1h',\n    initial_capital=100000.0,\n    use_checkpointing=True  # Resume if interrupted\n)\n\nmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"1-Year BTC Backtest\")\n```\n\n### Querying Provenance\n\n```python\nfrom quantagent.models import Signal, Order, Trade, Environment\n\n# Get all backtest orders with their triggering signals\norders = db.query(Order).filter(\n    Order.environment == Environment.BACKTEST\n).all()\n\nfor order in orders:\n    signal = order.trigger_signal\n    print(f\"Order {order.id} triggered by Signal {signal.id}\")\n    print(f\"  Model: {signal.model_provider}/{signal.model_name}\")\n    print(f\"  Confidence: {signal.confidence}\")\n\n# Get all signals and their resulting orders\nsignals = db.query(Signal).filter(\n    Signal.environment == Environment.BACKTEST\n).all()\n\nfor signal in signals:\n    if signal.order_id:\n        print(f\"Signal {signal.id} → Order {signal.order_id}\")\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Metrics\n\n### Viability Criteria (MVP)\n\nStrategy is considered viable if:\n- **Win Rate** ≥ 40%\n- **Sharpe Ratio** ≥ 1.0\n- **Max Drawdown** ≤ 15%\n\n### Interpretation\n\n| Metric | Good | Acceptable | Poor |\n|--------|------|-----------|------|\n| Win Rate | ≥ 50% | 40-50% | < 40% |\n| Profit Factor | ≥ 2.0 | 1.5-2.0 | < 1.5 |\n| Sharpe Ratio | ≥ 1.5 | 1.0-1.5 | < 1.0 |\n| Max Drawdown | ≤ 10% | 10-15% | > 15% |\n\n---\n\n## Metrics Calculation Details\n\n### Sharpe Ratio\n\n```python\n# Annualized Sharpe Ratio\nreturns = equity_curve.pct_change()\nexcess_return = returns.mean() - (risk_free_rate / periods_per_year)\nsharpe = (excess_return / returns.std()) * sqrt(periods_per_year)\n```\n\n**Periods per year**:\n- 1h: 252 × 6.5 = 1,638 (trading days × hours per day)\n- 4h: 252 × 1.625 = 410\n- 1d: 252\n- 1w: 52\n\n### Max Drawdown\n\n```python\n# Percentage-based drawdown\nrunning_max = equity_curve.expanding().max()\ndrawdown = (equity_curve - running_max) / running_max\nmax_drawdown = abs(drawdown.min())\n```\n\n### Profit Factor\n\n```python\n# Ratio of gross profit to gross loss\ntotal_wins = sum(pnl for pnl in trades if pnl > 0)\ntotal_losses = abs(sum(pnl for pnl in trades if pnl < 0))\nprofit_factor = total_wins / total_losses\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing\n\n### Unit Tests\n\n**DataProvider**: `tests/test_data_provider.py` (20 tests)\n- Structure validation\n- Cache-aside pattern\n- Gap detection\n- Symbol/timeframe mapping\n- Edge cases\n\n**Backtest**: `tests/test_backtest.py` (30+ tests)\n- Initialization\n- Date range generation\n- Metrics calculation (all formulas)\n- Decision parsing\n- Configuration snapshot\n\n### Integration Tests\n\n**Full Flow**: `tests/test_backtest_integration.py` (8 tests)\n- End-to-end backtest execution\n- Data fetching → Analysis → Execution → Metrics\n- Risk manager integration\n- Config snapshot reproducibility\n- Equity curve tracking\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\n# All backtesting tests\npytest tests/test_data_provider.py tests/test_backtest.py -v\n\n# Integration tests\npytest tests/test_backtest_integration.py -v\n```\n\n---\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### 1. Data Caching\n\nAlways use DataProvider for historical data:\n- First run: ~3 minutes (fetches from API)\n- Subsequent runs: ~10 seconds (reads from cache)\n\n### 2. Timeframe Selection\n\nRecommended timeframes by asset type:\n- **Crypto** (BTC): 1h or 4h\n- **Stocks** (SPX): 4h or 1d\n- **Commodities** (CL): 4h\n\n### 3. Date Ranges\n\nMinimum backtest periods:\n- **Development**: 1 month (quick validation)\n- **Testing**: 3 months (strategy validation)\n- **Production**: 1 year (robustness check)\n\n### 4. Configuration Management\n\nUse StrategyConfig model to persist profiles:\n\n```python\nfrom quantagent.models import StrategyConfig\n\n# Create profile\nconfig = StrategyConfig(\n    name=\"conservative_crypto\",\n    kind=\"combined\",\n    json_config={\n        'base_position_pct': 0.03,\n        'max_daily_loss_pct': 0.02,\n        # ...\n    }\n)\ndb.add(config)\ndb.commit()\n\n# Load profile\nconfig = db.query(StrategyConfig).filter_by(name=\"conservative_crypto\").first()\nbacktest = Backtest(config=config.json_config, ...)\n```\n\n### 5. Checkpointing\n\nEnable for long backtests:\n- Survives crashes\n- Resume from last checkpoint\n- Full execution history\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue: \"No data available\"\n\n**Cause**: Symbol not in cache, API fetch failed\n\n**Solution**:\n```python\n# Check cache status\nstats = provider.get_cache_stats(symbol='BTC')\nprint(stats)\n\n# Clear and re-fetch\nprovider.clear_cache(symbol='BTC')\nbacktest.run()\n```\n\n### Issue: \"Backtest too slow\"\n\n**Cause**: Cold cache, many API calls\n\n**Solution**:\n```python\n# Pre-populate cache\nfrom quantagent.data.provider import DataProvider\nprovider = DataProvider(db)\n\nfor symbol in ['BTC', 'SPX', 'CL']:\n    provider.get_ohlc(symbol, '1h', start, end)\n\n# Run backtest (now fast)\nbacktest.run()\n```\n\n### Issue: \"Zero trades executed\"\n\n**Cause**: Risk manager rejecting all trades\n\n**Solution**:\n```python\n# Check config\nprint(backtest.config)\n\n# Relax limits temporarily for testing\nconfig['max_position_pct'] = 0.50  # 50%\nconfig['max_daily_loss_pct'] = 0.20  # 20%\n```\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- **Code**: `quantagent/backtesting/backtest.py`\n- **Tests**: `tests/test_backtest.py`, `tests/test_backtest_integration.py`\n- **Example**: `examples/run_backtest.py`\n- **Requirements**: `docs/01_requirements/trading_system_requirements.md`\n- **Data Caching**: `docs/03_technical/data_caching_architecture.md`\n","numLines":668,"startLine":1,"totalLines":668}}}
