{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_013sXFSy6KryKwnHxwy3GAoe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me summarize the situation:\n\n**Current state (main branch):**\n- `Signal` model has NO `backtest_run_id` column\n- `BacktestRun` model has NO `replay_source_run_id` column\n- `backtest.py` has NO `run_replay()` method\n\n**Feature branch (QuantAgent-3o8):**\n- `BacktestRun` has `replay_source_run_id` FK (added by implementer)\n- `Signal` still has NO `backtest_run_id` FK (this is the bug)\n\n\n- `run_replay()` queries signals by symbol, timeframe, and date range only, then uses a map keyed by `(symbol, generated_at)` to look them up\n- When multiple runs overlap temporally or share assets, signals from different runs with identical `(symbol, generated_at)` pairs collide and overwrite each other in the map\n\nThe fix is to add a `backtest_run_id` foreign key to the `Signal` model so each signal is explicitly tied to its originating run, then update the signal creation methods to populate this field.\n\nI'll also need to modify `run_replay()` to filter by `backtest_run_id` instead of relying on the indirect query parameters, add an Alembic migration for the column, and write tests covering the overlapping run scenario.\n\nThis approach is clean because the foreign key makes signal ownership unambiguous regardless of time or symbol overlaps, and the filtering logic becomes straightforward.\n\nBetween adding the column directly versus trying to repurpose `thread_id`, Option A is the clear winner—`thread_id` serves a different purpose and isn't consistently populated anyway.\n\nNow I'm outlining the documentation structure I need to create, starting with requirements, planning, and design docs.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1625,"cache_read_input_tokens":63672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1625},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f08f8d0e-dfe1-47d6-abdf-e601734c006c","uuid":"cf2560ff-e3e7-4ffa-8d0b-955437295c92"}
